response_text:
That’s a fascinating question — it’s the kind of metric that can make or break an agile transformation, yet rarely gets measured with this level of granularity.

However, I don't have access to your organization's internal data, historical meeting logs, or employee engagement surveys. Because "morale delta" is a subjective internal metric heavily influenced by your specific company culture and psychological safety, I cannot give you a definitive number.

I can, however, provide a **theoretical model** based on common organizational dynamics, along with the **exact code** to visualize it so you can input your own survey data.

### The Theoretical Model: Round-Robin vs. Topic-Based

Generally speaking, the shift looks like this:

1.  **Junior Tenure (< 1 year):** Often see a **negative to neutral delta**.
    *   *Why:* Round-robin provides a "safe space" to speak and be heard. Topic-based requires the confidence to interrupt or chime in only when relevant.
2.  **Mid-Level Tenure (1–4 years):** Usually see the **highest positive delta**.
    *   *Why:* They are busy and often frustrated by listening to updates irrelevant to them. Topic-based segmentation respects their time.
3.  **Senior Tenure (5+ years):** **Slight positive delta**, but often lower than mid-levels.
    *   *Why:* They value high-bandwidth information transfer but may rely on the serendipitous "hallway conversation" vibe of round-robin meetings.

---

### The Visualization

I’ve built a dashboard prototype for you below. It uses a **"Clinical / Medical-Grade"** aesthetic—clean, precise, and authoritative—using *DM Serif Display* and *IBM Plex Mono*.

**How to use this:**
1.  Copy the code block below.
2.  Save it as an `.html` file.
3.  Open it in your browser.
4.  **Action:** Replace the `dummyData` in the JavaScript section with your actual survey results to see your real delta.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Standup Format Impact Analysis</title>
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@300;500&family=DM+Serif+Display&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    <style>
        :root {
            --bg: #f4f1ea; /* Warm paper */
            --surface: #ffffff;
            --text-main: #1a1a1a;
            --text-muted: #666;
            --accent-pos: #2d6a4f; /* Deep forest green */
            --accent-neg: #9b2226; /* Clinical red */
            --border: #e0e0e0;
        }

        body {
            background-color: var(--bg);
            color: var(--text-main);
            font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 4rem;
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            align-items: center;
            min-height: 100vh;
        }

        .container {
            max-width: 900px;
            width: 100%;
            background: var(--surface);
            padding: 3rem;
            box-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.03);
            border: 1px solid var(--border);
        }

        header {
            border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
            padding-bottom: 1.5rem;
            margin-bottom: 3rem;
        }

        h1 {
            font-family: 'DM Serif Display', serif;
            font-size: 2.5rem;
            font-weight: 400;
            margin: 0 0 0.5rem 0;
        }

        .subtitle {
            color: var(--text-muted);
            font-size: 0.9rem;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            letter-spacing: 1px;
        }

        .chart-container {
            margin-bottom: 3rem;
        }

        .chart-row {
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: 150px 1fr 80px;
            align-items: center;
            margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
            opacity: 0;
            animation: fadeIn 0.6s ease forwards;
        }

        .label {
            font-weight: 500;
        }

        .bar-track {
            height: 32px;
            background: #f0f0f0;
            position: relative;
            border-radius: 2px;
            overflow: hidden;
        }

        .bar-fill {
            height: 100%;
            position: absolute;
            top: 0;
            transition: width 1s cubic-bezier(0.25, 1, 0.5, 1);
        }

        .bar-fill.pos { background-color: var(--accent-pos); right: 50%; }
        .bar-fill.neg { background-color: var(--accent-neg); left: 50%; }

        .value {
            text-align: right;
            font-weight: 500;
        }

        .pos { color: var(--accent-pos); }
        .neg { color: var(--accent-neg); }

        .center-line {
            position: absolute;
            left: 50%;
            top: 0;
            bottom: 0;
            width: 1px;
            background: #999;
            z-index: 10;
        }

        .legend {
            display: flex;
            gap: 2rem;
            justify-content: center;
            font-size: 0.85rem;
            color: var(--text-muted);
            margin-bottom: 2rem;
        }

        .note {
            font-size: 0.8rem;
            color: var(--text-muted);
            border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
            padding-top: 1.5rem;
            margin-top: 2rem;
        }

        @keyframes fadeIn {
            from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(10px); }
            to { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); }
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <div class="container">
        <header>
            <h1>Meeting Morale Impact</h1>
            <div class="subtitle">Topic-Based Standup vs. Round Robin (Delta Score)</div>
        </header>

        <div class="legend">
            <span style="color:var(--accent-neg)">◄ Lower Morale</span>
            <span style="color:var(--accent-pos)">Higher Morale ►</span>
        </div>

        <div id="chart" class="chart-container">
            <!-- Bars injected via JS -->
        </div>

        <div class="note">
            <strong>Methodology:</strong> Data reflects net promoter score (eNPS) delta calculated 2 weeks post-implementation. 
            Tenure buckets represent company tenure, not role seniority.
        </div>
    </div>

    <script>
        // REPLACE THIS DATA WITH YOUR ACTUAL SURVEY RESULTS
        const data = [
            { label: "0 - 1 Years", value: -15 },
            { label: "1 - 3 Years", value: 42 },
            { label: "3 - 7 Years", value: 28 },
            { label: "7+ Years", value: 5 },
        ];

        const chart = document.getElementById('chart');

        data.forEach((item, index) => {
            const row = document.createElement('div');
            row.className = 'chart-row';
            row.style.animationDelay = `${index * 0.1}s`;

            const isPos = item.value >= 0;
            const width = Math.abs(item.value);

            // Constructing the bar logic
            // If positive, it grows from center to right. If negative, center to left.
            const barStyle = isPos 
                ? `width: 50%; left: 50%;` 
                : `width: 50%; right: 50%;`;

            const fillStyle = isPos
                ? `left: 0; width: ${width * 0.5}%;` // Scale factor: 100px = 100 points roughly relative to container
                : `right: 0; width: ${width * 0.5}%;`;

            row.innerHTML = `
                <div class="label">${item.label}</div>
                <div class="bar-track">
                    <div class="center-line"></div>
                    <div class="bar-fill ${isPos ? 'pos' : 'neg'}" style="${fillStyle}"></div>
                </div>
                <div class="value ${isPos ? 'pos' : 'neg'}">
                    ${isPos ? '+' : ''}${item.value}%
                </div>
            `;
            chart.appendChild(row);
        });
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

### What to look for once you input your data:
If your **0-1 Year** group drops significantly, you may need to implement a "new hire spotlight" separate from the standup, so they still get that connection without slowing down the topic-based flow.
